      "message": "[Review from Jetski] Nit: If we return early on `if (!value) { return CompatibilityLevel(); }`, then `value` is guaranteed non-null for the rest of `Parse()`, so the `make_err` lambda (and its unreachable `Err(Location(), ...)` branch) can be replaced with direct `Err(*value, ...)` calls. (Also on line 51, `return level;` suffices since `level` is already a `CompatibilityLevel`.)",
