      "writtenOn": "2026-11-25T06:33:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Review from Jetski] Negative values (e.g. `-1`, `-5`) currently fall into this branch and report `\"compatibility_level -1 is no longer supported.\"` even though negative levels were never valid. In addition, when `kMin \u003d\u003d 0`, the loop below runs 0 times and leaves a dangling empty `\"Changes required to upgrade:\\n\"` section (and once `kMin \u003e 0`, a negative value like `-5` would list upgrade steps starting from level 0).\n\nConsider handling `level.level_ \u003c 0` explicitly with a separate error (e.g. `\"Invalid compatibility_level ... (must be \u003e\u003d 0).\"`), and only appending `\"Changes required to upgrade:\\n\"` when there is at least one upgrade step to list. (Note: `ParseLastUnsupported` in `compatibility_level_unittest.cc` would need to be adjusted accordingly while `kLastUnsupported \u003c 0`.)",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "f4e848cde709dbff1be587070402a93849bf6061",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
    },
