      "writtenOn": "2026-11-25T06:33:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Review from Jetski] Because `std::array` uses aggregate initialization with an explicit size, forgetting to add a description when introducing a new `Level` (or accidentally deleting an old entry when removing a deprecated `Level`) will silently default-initialize missing trailing entries to empty `std::string_view{}` without a compile error, potentially shifting indices or printing empty upgrade instructions.\n\nConsider adding a `static_assert` verifying that every entry in `kCompatibilityLevels` is non-empty (or deducing the size from the initializer list and `static_assert`ing it equals `static_cast\u003csize_t\u003e(CompatibilityLevel::kCurrent)`). It would also help to note in the removal process comment above (lines 32–38) that old entries in `kCompatibilityLevels` must be kept so indices continue to align with `Level` values.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "f4e848cde709dbff1be587070402a93849bf6061",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
